From 5815f14be38d2ea1c16e8a6faf8fa466507973fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:42:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] resolve: from 2018 the implicit `extern crate std`/`core` is
 not nameable by a path, a glob import of `std` wins

pyo3 0.28.3 (py314-pydantic_core 2.46.5) src/conversions/num_bigint.rs:52-55 `use crate::{conversion::IntoPyObject,
std::num::nb_index, ..}`: "Unable to resolve `use` target crate::std::num::nb_index". pyo3's conversions/mod.rs has
`pub(crate) mod std;` and lib.rs `pub use crate::conversions::*;`, so the root gets `std` = that module by a glob.
rustc injects `extern crate std;` (`core` for #![no_std]) with def-site hygiene from 2018: no path (`crate::std`,
`self::std`, a glob of the root) names it, it only provides `#[macro_use]` and the extern prelude. mrustc's injected
item was an ordinary private root item, which beats a glob import, so `crate::std` was libstd. Not a regression.

expand/mod.cpp: the injected item carries a `#std_injection` marker attribute (no source attribute can spell it).
resolve: from 2018 the index leaves it out of the root module and `use` resolution skips it (the item scan of
Resolve_Use_GetBinding__mod and the local-shadow check of the extern prelude). It still feeds `#[macro_use]` and the
extern prelude (g_implicit_crates, filled from the item during expansion), so `std::..` / `use std::..` resolve as
before. 2015 is unchanged (rustc's item is nameable there too). Rust 1.90's library sources (rust-src) and the mrustc
1.90 source patch have no `crate::core`/`self::core`/`crate::std` path, so libstd/liballoc are unaffected; a 2018+
crate that wrote `crate::std::..` without such an item is now rejected, as by rustc (E0432).

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context)
